1. Log in to Cloudflare

npx wrangler login
A browser window opens. Click Allow.

2. Create the database

npx wrangler d1 create python-for-kids
It prints a database_id. Open wrangler.toml and replace 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000 with it.

3. Load the 17 topics into it

npm run db:migrate:remote
4. Set the admin password and session secret

npx wrangler pages secret put ADMIN_PASSWORD --project-name python-tutorial-for-kids
npx wrangler pages secret put SESSION_SECRET --project-name python-tutorial-for-kids
Each one asks you to type a value.

ADMIN_PASSWORD: pick a strong password. This is what you'll log in with on the live site.
SESSION_SECRET: generate a random value with this command and paste it in:

node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
If you get "project not found", your Pages project has a different name. Find it at dash.cloudflare.com → Workers & Pages, then use that name in these commands and in wrangler.toml.

5. Check the build settings
On dash.cloudflare.com, open your project → Settings → Build. They must be:

Root directory: frontend
Build command: npm run build
Output directory: dist
6. Commit and push

cd ..
git add -A
git commit -m "Add admin panel with Cloudflare D1 backend"
git push
Cloudflare rebuilds the site automatically, which takes about 1–2 minutes.

7. Check it works
https://python-tutorial-for-kids.pages.dev: the site should load as before.
https://python-tutorial-for-kids.pages.dev/admin: log in with the password from step 4.
